    },
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Seville sits on the banks of the Guadalquivir in southern Spain. It is the capital of Andalusia and one of the warmest cities in Europe.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Moorish builders left the Real Alcázar and the Giralda, which began as a minaret and now serves as the cathedral bell tower. Plaza de España came later, built for the 1929 Ibero-American Exposition. Across the river, Triana keeps its own tapas bars and ceramic workshops.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Spring and autumn suit walking. Summer afternoons are hot, so the city keeps late hours and eats dinner after 9 pm.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
